+# Hegel property-based testing report: `brotli` (dropbox/rust-brotli)
+
+Tests were added to the existing test file `src/enc/test.rs` (module
+`hegel_props`, `#[cfg(feature = "std")]`), using `hegeltest` 0.28.2, added with
+`cargo add --dev hegeltest --ignore-rust-version` (the crate pins
+`rust-version = "1.59.0"`, hegeltest needs 1.86 — a maintainer decision if
+upstreamed). The crate is edition 2015 and `#![no_std]` with a default `std`
+feature, so `#[cfg(test)] extern crate hegel;` was added to `src/lib.rs` and
+the test module imports `std::string::{String, ToString}` explicitly.
+`.hegel/` was added to `.gitignore`.
+
+Two shared composite generators drive most properties:
+
+- `enc_cfgs()` — the configuration pattern: quality 0–11, `q9_5` (quality ≥ 10),
+  lgwin 10–24, lgblock auto (0) or 16–24, mode generic/text/font, magic number,
+  size hint on/off, `disable_literal_context_modeling`. Returned as a compact
+  `Debug`-printable `EncCfg` struct (rather than the 30-field
+  `BrotliEncoderParams`) so counterexamples stay readable.
+- `payloads()` — structured payloads: 0–6 pieces, each a single-byte run
+  (≤ 2 KiB), a repeated small chunk (LZ back-reference food), Unicode text, or
+  arbitrary bytes. Sizes bounded (~12 KiB max) to protect the test's time
+  budget at quality 11, not the library's contract.
+
+## Properties tested
+
+Ten properties, plus one deterministic pinned-bug reproducer.
+
+1. **`test_hegel_oneshot_roundtrip`** — one-shot `BrotliCompress` →
+   `BrotliDecompress` is the identity for every generated configuration and
+   payload.
+2. **`test_hegel_compressor_writer_streaming_roundtrip`** — `CompressorWriter`
+   with drawn internal buffer size (1–8192), a drawn write-chunk schedule and
+   drawn intermediate `flush()` points still produces a stream that decodes to
+   the input.
+3. **`test_hegel_compressor_reader_streaming_roundtrip`** — `CompressorReader`
+   (Read adapter) with drawn internal buffer size and drawn read granularity
+   produces a stream that decodes to the input.
+4. **`test_hegel_decompressor_reader_matches_oneshot`** — the `Decompressor`
+   Read adapter, driven with drawn buffer size and read granularity, agrees
+   with the one-shot decompressor and with the original input.
+5. **`test_hegel_decompressor_writer_streaming_roundtrip`** —
+   `DecompressorWriter` fed a valid stream in drawn write chunks reconstructs
+   the input and closes cleanly.
+6. **`test_hegel_decompress_arbitrary_bytes_never_panics`** — decompressing
+   arbitrary bytes (one-shot and via the Read adapter) returns an error or
+   data but never panics.
+7. **`test_hegel_truncated_stream_errors`** — a strict prefix of a valid
+   compressed stream never decompresses successfully (the terminating ISLAST
+   metablock cannot be complete), and never panics. Cut point drawn over the
+   whole stream, including 0.
+8. **`test_hegel_bitflip_never_panics`** — decompressing a valid stream with
+   one drawn bit flipped never panics (it may legally succeed: brotli has no
+   integrity check, so success is not asserted to be an error).
+9. **`test_hegel_custom_dictionary_roundtrip`** — compressing with a custom
+   dictionary (`BrotliCompressCustomIoCustomDict`) and decompressing with the
+   same dictionary (`brotli_decompressor::BrotliDecompressCustomDict`) is the
+   identity. The payload generator deliberately splices slices of the drawn
+   dictionary into the input so dictionary back-references are actually
+   exercised.
+10. **`test_hegel_brocatli_concat_roundtrip`** — 1–3 payloads compressed with
+    `catable = true` under independently drawn configurations, concatenated
+    with `BroCatli` (drawn output buffer size 1–4096, window pinned to 24 —
+    see Unsound properties), decompress to the concatenation of the payloads.
+    Empty payloads are excluded because of the real bug below.
+
+Pinned reproducer: **`test_brocatli_empty_stream_after_q1_stream_known_failure`**
+— deterministic plain `#[test]` documenting the BroCatli bug found by
+property 10 before the exclusion was added. Expected to FAIL until the bug is
+fixed.
+
+## Test results
+
+- All ten properties pass at the default 100 cases and at a 10× exploratory
+  run (`test_cases = 1000`, since reverted).
+- Liveness was verified by temporarily inverting an assertion in property 1;
+  hegel found and shrank a counterexample (4-byte input), then the change was
+  reverted.
+- The pinned reproducer fails deterministically on every run:
+  `BroCatli produced a stream that fails to decompress: Custom { kind: UnexpectedEof, ... }`.
+- The full pre-existing suite (`cargo test --no-fail-fast`) still passes:
+  lib tests 48 passed / 1 failed (the intentional pin), bin tests 100 passed.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+**1. BroCatli emits a non-decodable stream (reporting Success) when an empty
+catable stream follows a stream with a particular final-byte bit pattern.**
+Real bug, pinned by `test_brocatli_empty_stream_after_q1_stream_known_failure`
+(src/enc/test.rs). Hegel's shrunk counterexample: first stream = quality-1,
+lgwin-10, catable encoding of the 22 bytes `b"0001" + b"0"*18` (compressed
+bytes end `0xA1 0x01`); second stream = the empty catable stream `[0xA1, 0x01]`.
+`BroCatli::new()` + `stream()` + `finish()` report success, but the output ends
+`[0x21, 0x80, 0x80]` where the valid single-stream output ends `[0xA1, 0x01]`,
+and decompression fails with `UnexpectedEof`. Scoping experiments:
+
+- First-stream quality 0, 2, or 5 with the same inputs: OK.
+- Same first stream followed by a *non-empty* stream: OK.
+- Same pair but concatenated under `BroCatli::new_with_window_size(24)` with a
+  third non-empty stream appended: OK (the header rewrite changes the bit
+  alignment), so the trigger is the alignment of the previous stream's final
+  ISLAST bits when the appended stream contains *only* window bits + ISLAST —
+  i.e. a bit-surgery edge case in `flush_previous_stream`/`stream` in
+  `src/concat/mod.rs`.
+
+Both inputs decompress correctly on their own (asserted in the pinned test),
+so this is silent corruption of valid inputs by the concatenation tool.
+
+**2. Observation (surprising interaction, not asserted as a bug):** the
+encoder silently raises the effective window to ≥ 18 when quality is 0 or 1
+(`lgwin = max(lgwin, 18)` in `ensure_initialized`), so with
+`BroCatli::new()` (window inferred from the first file) appending a
+quality-0/1 stream after a quality-≥2 lgwin-10 stream fails with
+`WindowSizeLargerThanPreviousFile` even though every stream was requested with
+the same `lgwin = 10`. The error code exists for this and
+`new_with_window_size` is the documented escape hatch, so the property was
+redesigned around it rather than pinned, but it is a foot-gun worth mentioning
+upstream alongside bug 1.
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+- **BroCatli with an inferred window and per-stream drawn lgwin** (first
+  version of property 10) — unsound: `WindowSizeLargerThanPreviousFile` is a
+  legitimate documented error path, and the quality-0/1 window bump above
+  means even "same lgwin for every stream" does not avoid it. Replaced with
+  `BroCatli::new_with_window_size(24)` (24 is an upper bound for every
+  generated stream), which also exercises the header-rewrite path.
+- **Bit-flipped streams must fail to decompress** — never asserted: brotli has
+  no checksum, so a flipped bit can legally produce a different valid stream.
+  The committed property asserts no-panic only.
+- **Byte-identical output between streaming adapters and one-shot
+  compression** — deliberately not asserted; flush points and buffer sizes
+  legitimately change the emitted stream. Semantic (roundtrip) equality is
+  asserted instead.
+- Experimental modes 3–6 (`BROTLI_FORCE_*_PRIOR`) were left out of the
+  configuration generator (only generic/text/font are generated); they are
+  reachable via `set_parameter` but appear to be internal/experimental IR
+  knobs, and asserting roundtrip for them was not evidence-grounded. A
+  follow-up could probe them separately.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+- The edition-2015 + `no_std` guidance in the Rust reference was accurate and
+  sufficient: `#[cfg(test)] extern crate hegel;` at the crate root plus
+  `use std::string::{String, ToString};` in the test module was all that was
+  needed (this crate's `#[macro_use] extern crate std;` already provided
+  `format!`/`vec!`). The MSRV `--ignore-rust-version` note matched exactly.
+- "Generate configurations, not just payloads" was the highest-value pattern
+  here — the shrunk BroCatli counterexample needed quality *1 specifically*
+  plus an empty payload, a combination no canned-config test would hit.
+- The "drawing schedules for streaming APIs" pattern (bounded chunk-size
+  schedule, cycled) worked directly for all four adapter properties.
+- A pattern worth adding to the skill: when a crate's config struct has a huge
+  `Debug` representation (30 fields here), draw a compact purpose-built config
+  struct and convert, so counterexamples print small. This made the failure
+  immediately readable.
+- Shrinking quality was excellent: the initial failure (3 streams, mixed
+  configs, multi-KiB payloads) shrank to 2 streams / 22-byte + empty payloads /
+  `out_buf_size = 1`, which made triage (a dozen targeted matrix experiments)
+  fast.
